t(20, 675, """She was barred from entry for holding a foreign passport without having obtained a visa .. and (the Ummah becomes great), as came in the noble hadith in the words of the Prophet ﷺ ..

I understand it thus: no exceptions in an Ummah that respects itself and fears for its sacred national security .. And "the Ummah becomes great", the phrase the Prophet ﷺ said, I understand to mean that whoever clings to the Western passport will go on being treated as a visitor with no citizenship rights, so long as he does not replace his passport and renounce his Western nationality by an official letter from the body that issued the passport, stripping him of that nationality. "The Ummah becomes great" means the Ummah becomes great. This is how the texts from the Prophet ﷺ are understood.""")

t(20, 2265, """The end of the era of the Western passport! Visa required!""")

