t(24, 160, """O Allah, be with her, grant her success and help her .. every mother who struggles to save her children from a corrupt father who strives to corrupt them, or a violent, merciless father who has destroyed his children or strives to destroy them, driven by Iblis, while he does not understand and thinks he is doing good, or a father who does not fear Allah in the well-known necessities and clear rules of sound child-rearing, or a father who tries to take his young children to lands where there are moral dangers for them in their adolescence.""")

t(24, 1785, """May Allah relieve his distress and lift his worry (the sheikh in years .. Wagdi Ghoneim) .. I disagree with him on dozens of files .. I disagree with him over how easily he leaps to conclusions that lead to classifying the other as a disbeliever, in certain files and issues, not generalising over all his statements. I disagree with him over calling for revolutions, and I disagree with him over rebelling against the ruler, and I see that as a red-line error that neither a religious sheikh nor anyone else should call for. But I always saw him as a stranded man who deserves help from any society or country he settles in .. A sick, elderly man, a wayfarer. My disagreement with him over everything he calls for did not remove from me the feeling of compassion for him as an elderly person, since as long as awareness countering these mistaken calls is spread by the wise and the sensible in the Ummah, calls like these do not harm Arab and Muslim societies .. I prayed against the sheikh 4 or 5 years ago, in words I do not recall .. The reason I prayed against him was his close relationship with Saber Mashhour .. For 3 years, or perhaps two full years, the sheikh did not want to come out and respond to Saber Mashhour over Saber Mashhour's wrecking of the religion, and kept an unacceptable silence about him! Saber Mashhour insulted the Household of the Messenger of Allah and the sheikh was silent!! He attacked many of the noble Prophetic hadiths and the sheikh was silent .. Then when Saber Mashhour's audacity grew and reached a point that brought many out to speak about his corruption, the sheikh came out timidly, without his usual state of anger that we know, and spoke to Saber calmly! Where is the anger for Allah, for His Messenger and for his Household? Where is loyalty and disavowal? For fifty years the sheikh has been telling us about loyalty and disavowal! And when one day, years ago, the Strip thought of making a truce, he came out and accused them of betraying Allah, His Messenger and the Ummah! So the sheikh rushes to respond at once; why then did the offence against the religion by Saber Mashhour take between two and 3 years to be answered? A question addressed to the sheikh alone. I prayed against the sheikh in that period as a Muslim who sees anger for Allah Almighty and His Messenger in some issues, while in other issues there is silence!

Today I pray for this elderly man, homeless in Allah's earth, because I know the meaning of homelessness .. I prayed against you 4 or""")

t(25, 150, """5 years ago, and the prayer was against you, not for you. Today I pray for you, as a Muslim who knows you the way people know you from YouTube, that He relieve your worry over your residency, which has been refused you for years, and your remaining in this state for years, which by Allah is no easy state; along with my prayers that you review your thinking. For you interpret the verses on loyalty and disavowal out of their place, you do not understand politics, you do not understand interests, and you know nothing of what goes on behind the scenes; then you come out and interfere in extremely sensitive issues of a people under occupation whose distress for 75 years none knows but their Lord alone, and that was before the Flood.

Likewise, perhaps the prayer of someone other than me struck you, for an injustice you committed in how you dealt with loyalty and disavowal: you took from it what does not embarrass you and left what embarrasses you. Loyalty and disavowal for the Prophet and his family ought not to embarrass you. This is your Prophet, and these are his lineage and blood, whom you kept silent from defending for about 3 years; then you came out with great timidity and great softness, saying to Saber: O Saber, shame, as though he had wronged a clover factory! I wondered at you, being in the same country with you at the time, saying: what is with this sheikh who speaks of nothing but loyalty and disavowal, why does he not disavow?! Why does he not disavow the wrong? Why is he silent? Silent about Saber's corruption with the silence of the graves?! For two years, man, or more, not for months? I am not the only one in this world who followed that from you! Perhaps it was the prayers of many; why must I confine the matter to a prayer I made in anger at one silent about the truth, when the angry were many that day, and at every time? People are angry at the one from whom they expect the truth to be spoken; as for the one from whom speaking the truth is not expected, hands are washed of him and no one is angry at him, because he does not present himself to Muslim society as a caller to the truth! But the one who presents himself to Muslim society as a defender of the truth, society will not accept from him taking half the truth and leaving half!

This is a story that may be related to your suffering now for years. Just as that prayer was anger for Allah Almighty at your abandoning loyalty and disavowal in matters of religion about which silence is not right, so praying for you, for the relief of your worry, is a duty on us all. I will devote a prayer to you in the depth of the night, Allah Almighty willing. The prayer against you was for Allah the Great, and the prayer for you is for Allah the Great, whether from me or from other Muslims who rise and pray at night while people sleep. As a stranded, elderly Muslim; no personal enmity towards your person. But whoever comes out to the people, takes the lead and speaks must be held to account for his positions. O Allah, relieve this sheikh's distress and grant him a way out of the problem of his refused residency.""")

