t(37, 970, """For 1447 years Muslim kingdoms rose and Muslim kingdoms fell, and powerful states ruled the Islamic world! What prevented them from taking Bayt al-Maqdis as the seat of rule? They took Baghdad, Cairo, Damascus, Istanbul, North Africa and others as great centres of a long, extended rule that lasted centuries, except Damascus, less than a century. So who prevented them from declaring Jerusalem the capital of their rule? No one prevented them. Today they begrudge this flower blooming even once in the entire Islamic era! It will bloom in spite of your shu'ubiyya, which the Prophet ﷺ commanded you to disavow! This wronged city .. wronged by Nebuchadnezzar, then by the Romans, then by the Crusades, then today by those you know, has the right to address the world, even once in its history, so that all people are brought to it without distinction. So I say to the shu'ubis: if you had sense you would understand that it is your city too, that it concerns you, and that you have a share in it; so leave that rotten thing .. For you will be shocked by what is coming, and perhaps the intensive care beds in the hospitals will not cover the number of all these shu'ubi nationalists who have disowned the injunctions of their Prophet ﷺ.""")

